<header class="article_header">
<p class="eyebrow">LOCAL SURVEILLANCE · MCHENRY COUNTY / HUNTLEY, ILLINOIS</p>
<h1>McHenry County surveillance, agency by agency.</h1>
<p class="article_deck">This file documents surveillance systems tied to local agencies through government reports, procurement records, public meetings, public records, and clearly identified secondary sources.</p>
</header>

<section>
<p class="eyebrow">HUNTLEY POLICE DEPARTMENT</p>
<h2>ALPR, vehicle fingerprinting, body cameras, and drones.</h2>
<div class="finding_grid">
<article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>17 Flock ALPRs</h3><p>Huntley approved a four-year Flock Safety lease in 2023 for 17 license-plate readers at a reported total cost of $187,150, intended for major thoroughfares entering and leaving the village.</p></article>
<article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Vehicle fingerprinting</h3><p>Huntley's presentation described searchable plate number, make, model, color, and unique features including bumper stickers, decals, and roof racks, and described Flock as producing leads through a vehicle's “fingerprint.”</p></article>
<article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Axon body cameras</h3><p>Public documentation reports Huntley outfitted officers with Axon body-worn cameras in 2023 as part of the same period of technology upgrades.</p></article>
<article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Two police drones</h3><p>Illinois' State Fiscal Year 2024 Freedom from Drone Surveillance Act report lists Huntley Police as owning two drones and reports 38 flights during the reporting period.</p></article>
</div>
<div class="evidence_box">
<span class="status_label">SOURCE NOTE</span>
<p>The Flock deployment and vehicle-attribute description are supported by Huntley's public-board record and contemporaneous reporting. Drone inventory and flight totals come from Illinois' statewide statutory drone report.</p>
</div>
