<section>
<p class="eyebrow">MCHENRY COUNTY SHERIFF'S OFFICE</p>
<h2>ALPR, drones, and networked video evidence.</h2>
<div class="finding_grid">
<article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Body + in-car video</h3><p>A McHenry County project report allocated $2.09 million for body cameras, in-car cameras, and Tasers for patrol deputies and states the equipment works together on one system with material stored in Evidence.com.</p></article>
<article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Two sheriff's drones</h3><p>The SFY 2024 statewide drone report is indexed as showing two McHenry County Sheriff's Office drones and 24 flights during the reporting period.</p></article>
<article><span class="status_label">SECONDARY-SOURCE CONFIRMED</span><h3>ALPR use since 2022</h3><p>The EFF Atlas of Surveillance records McHenry County Sheriff's Office use of automated license-plate readers beginning in 2022, based on local reporting. The underlying sheriff procurement or policy record is not in the current archive.</p></article>
<article><span class="status_label">UNKNOWN</span><h3>ALPR vendor and current configuration</h3><p>The material currently collected here does not establish the Sheriff's current ALPR vendor, reader count, locations, retention configuration, sharing network, or authorized-user count.</p></article>
</div>
